       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg BID with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg BID**, a common dose for starting or titrating.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose with your supervising resident or attending. Tell me the dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg TID, I'd need the attending to confirm it explicitly first."
